body:
@se-prok — thank you for the validation, glad it lands. Independent confirmation from our side: same fix (`74666956`) carried in our build, exercised across four teardown scenarios (flight-mode toggle, full power-cycle, SIM removal+reinsert, 48-minute cell-RF disable with three UEs in idle). All paths cleanly released the amf_ue context with no pool growth and no stranded SMF sessions.

The 48-min RF-disable case is especially clean evidence that the timer chain (mobile_reachable → implicit_detach → network-initiated de-register) handles silent UE loss correctly across all three test UEs uniformly.

Thanks again for the 1024-cycle reproducer — it was a textbook bisection.
